# ─── Backend .dockerignore ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Practical 11 Supplementary: Exclude files from Docker build context
#
# The build context is everything Docker sends to the daemon when building.
# Large or irrelevant files in the context slow down every build significantly.
#
# node_modules  — MUST be excluded. Platform-specific binaries won't work
#                 across OS boundaries. npm install runs inside the container.
# .env          — MUST be excluded. Secrets are injected at runtime via
#                 docker-compose.yml environment section or Docker secrets.
#                 Never bake .env values into an image layer.
# .git          — Not needed inside the container; wastes build context size.

node_modules
.env
.git
*.log
npm-debug.log*
dist
.nyc_output
coverage
